{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Quick_and_easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Quick and easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Solution_1_Rigorously)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Solution 1 Rigorously)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_(Short)_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video (Short) Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are arbitrarily separated into five groups of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers each. The median of each group is identified. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> equal the median of the five medians. What is the least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/3982984781bbf2eae1cc46d8b193dc1d201a5868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }9 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }10 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }12 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }13 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"392\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4be1c5f42375f148768eb7aa7597a9a9d5b0196.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]      unitsize(5mm);            fill((0,2) -- (3,2) -- (3,5) -- (0,5) -- cycle, mediumgray+opacity(0.4));      draw(box((0,0),(5,5)));      draw((0,1) -- (5,1));      draw((0,2) -- (5,2));      draw((0,3) -- (5,3));      draw((0,4) -- (5,4));      draw((1,0) -- (1,5));      draw((2,0) -- (2,5));      draw((3,0) -- (3,5));      draw((4,0) -- (4,5));            draw((6,2.5) -- (7,2.5),arrow=ArcArrow(SimpleHead));            fill((8,2) -- (11,2) -- (11,5) -- (8,5) -- cycle, mediumgray+opacity(0.4));      draw(box((8,0),(13,5)));      draw((8,1) -- (13,1));      draw((8,2) -- (13,2));      draw((8,3) -- (13,3));      draw((8,4) -- (13,4));      draw((9,0) -- (9,5));      draw((10,0) -- (10,5));      draw((11,0) -- (11,5));      draw((12,0) -- (12,5));      draw(box((10,2),(11,3)), black+2bp);            label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(10.5,2.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"308\" height=\"122\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Consider using a five by five square table to solve this problem. The rows represent the five groups, the center column is the median of each group and the center square cell is the least possible value of \\(M\\). The only numbers that really matter is the ones in the shaded area, the rest can be ignored. In order to find the least possible value of \\(M\\) the smallest numbers, \\(1 ... 9\\), need to be in these nine square cells. \\(9\\) is the smallest number that is able to satisfy both median of a group and median of five medians. Final answer, the least possible value of \\(M\\) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02cab8c0df01f06c179dee813b86859829d6566d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}~9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" /> ~TutorJack\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Quick_and_easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Quick_and_easy)\">Solution 2 (Quick and easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Quick and easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a group has median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, then we must have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the numbers in that group are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d6fda183d8f7d002a1dedcac05dc9d6c5f1e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" />. Since there are 5 different groups, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> groups must have a median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c1445958466852bba52e8314575cea6dde0df6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />, so there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d130c03ebc6720f2f3723c168c75cacf89e4465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot3=9$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> numbers that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c1445958466852bba52e8314575cea6dde0df6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Since there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c1445958466852bba52e8314575cea6dde0df6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> at minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adca556acb28117d0e3130712a6dd8329c3a2909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" /> ~Baihly2024\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Solution_1_Rigorously.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Solution_1_Rigorously)\">Solution 3 (Solution 1 Rigorously)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Solution 1 Rigorously)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the groupings be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad190a489e441e5236adca60f231adf3f410596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_1, G_2, \\dots, G_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. Let the medians of each of the groupings be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe1089c7d48e8d434bf8e8c639cd3506d0026a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, m_2, m_3, m_4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aed44bcbb6183a6fdd4d26c79021ee972e131b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> in that order. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the median of those medians. Then, we wish to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. This can be possible if we have three elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db8d2c3b6325306a87e8a10b0e5358afb2f23eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, three elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a742fa7110e3779fe13d9b3014b0e2ad6606c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and three elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e592e7c572098aaa72922f31a260997722aab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> less than an equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are there (as the last number itself is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />). Thus, the smallest way to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c36c0c2bc673a7265eb304fc8f0f82a42b08c697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, \\dots, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest of these, and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374ad4e9adc96666cde62dd31911b54d38e83c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you want to prove a solution one of the easiest ways is just to list an example of it.\nA median has to be greater than the first two numbers of the group.\nThen we just list the groups out.\nThis includes:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n( 1,2,3,16,17) ,\\ ( 4,5,6,18,19) ,\\ ( 7,8,9,20,21) ,\\ ( 10,11,12,22,23) ,\\ ( 13,14,15,24,25) &amp; &amp; \n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Then according to this triple we are able to find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd9621c87774cb6ff5d10575efe6c525f2efd06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Lynn403\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gWITN0xu8lc\">https://youtu.be/gWITN0xu8lc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_.28Short.29_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_.28ANIMATED.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_(Short)_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED!)\">Video (Short) Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index